# Zone 1, room 8: Attack-cancel landing (BUILD.md s5 tech 8: "landing never interrupts an attack.
# Taught by a boss with a short window"). Grey box, not art.
#
# The room is a staircase of three drops, 60 x 34 tiles, west door high and east door low:
#   platform A  x 0..480    floor y 480   (west door: opening y 352..480, arrival x 74)
#   platform B  x 480..960  floor y 576   drop 96 u, 16 f of fall
#   platform C  x 960..1440 floor y 768   drop 192 u, 21 f of fall
#   platform D  x 1440..1920 floor y 960  drop 192 u, 21 f of fall (east door: opening y 832..960)
# Ash runs at 540 u/s (9 u/f), so a drop carries her about 150 u (B) or 190 u (C, D) before the
# floor: the landing is where a dummy 76 u past it can just be reached. A dummy is a stand-in for
# the boss with a short window (Phase 1 has no boss): a one-hit (hp=10) training dummy.
#   B: dummy at 706, no attack. The safe first encounter: strike on the way down, land mid-strike,
#      watch the strike go on to its last frame with no landing lag (Taper side 1: 2 f startup,
#      4 f active, 8 f recovery, 68 u reach, so a press 4 f before the landing is live on the
#      landing's two last airborne frames and its two first grounded ones).
#   C and D: dummies at 1235 and 1730 with an unparryable (red=1) swing, so the strike has to be
#      the answer, not the parry (a press near a white swing parries it). Telegraph 24 f, 4 f
#      active, 20 f recovery, 64 u in front of the dummy. They are ambushers (trigger=284 and
#      293): the swing opens when Ash reaches the ledge, 284 u from C (293 from D, 9 u before its
#      ledge), and its first active tick is 23 f later, the tick after the teaching route's
#      landing. (Placed after the merge of the movement and combat fixes: side 1's 8-frame recoil
#      slows the run 1 u a frame while it lasts, so the teaching route reaches each ledge 9 u
#      later than it did, 16 u later by drop 3; C stands 9 u nearer and D 9 u further, with D's
#      trigger 9 u longer, so that the route's kill falls on the landing frame again, a tick
#      before the swing. The runs with no strike before them have no recoil, are 9 u ahead, and
#      meet C's swing on their landing tick, not after it; they are hit all the same.) The swing is tied to where Ash is,
#      not to the clock, so nothing she did before (a kill's hitstop, a wait) moves it against
#      her landing. The strike pressed 4 f before the landing kills the dummy on the landing
#      frame; one pressed on the landing frame is live 2 f later, the swing lands first, is hit
#      for a heart and the strike is broken, whatever the run before.
#
# What the room proves and what it does not (review F1 to F3): with fixtures, the way down that
# never stops (tests/replay/zone1/08_strike_on_the_way_down: 3 drops, 0 hearts lost, 210 f) costs
# no heart, and the plain alternatives each cost one: no strike (08_control_no_strike), a strike
# pressed on the landing (08_control_strike_after_landing, 08_control_land_then_strike), waiting
# before the run (08_control_wait) and one dash (08_control_one_dash). It is NOT enforced against
# dashing: a dash (20 u/f) outruns a 24 f telegraph, so two dashes cross with 5 hearts in 174 f
# (08_gap_two_dashes), faster than the teaching route. A dummy is no wall and Phase 1 has no boss
# that blocks a door; when the boss with the short window exists, its door closes the gap and the
# gap fixture becomes a control. Until then tech 8 is taught here, not enforced (PROGRESS.md).
room zone1/08_attack_cancel_landing
size 60 34
spawn 74 480
tiles
